    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0111" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p1/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.01/11–2149:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bruce</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-21T20:00:00+01:00">November 21,
                            1949—8 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4883. Baeyens<anchor n="1" xml:id="d78-f1"/> tells us MacDonald<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d78-f2"/> informed Pignon that he was strongly recommending to
                    London British recognition of Bao Dai government. While MacDonald believes it
                    preferable that British recognition follow similar action by some SEA nations (he mentioned Ceylon and Siam), he does
                    not feel that British need wait if there are signs SEA recognitions will be delayed.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 4883; repeated London 839; Department pass Saigon 155.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d78-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d78-f1" n="1" xml:id="d78-f1-content">
                <p>Ferdinand Jacques M. G. Baeyens was in charge of Asian affairs at the French
                    Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d78-f2" n="2" xml:id="d78-f2-content">
                <p>Malcolm MacDonald, Commissioner-General for the United Kingdom in Southeast Asia,
                    with rank of Ambassador and headquarters at Singapore, was on a visit to
                    Indochina.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d78-f3" n="3" xml:id="d78-f3-content">
                <p>This was done November 22.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
